{"name":"Deer Valley","hex":"#c7a485","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ruminant mammal with hooves and often antlers, of the family Cervidae, or one of several similar animals from related families of the order Artiodactyla, such as the musk deer or mouse deer.","Such a mammal that is in the family Cervidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deer"},{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deer Valley","blocks":[{"text":"Deer Valley is a ski-only resort in the Wasatch Range, located 36 miles (58 km) east of Salt Lake City, in Park City, Utah, United States, where snowboarding is prohibited."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d9/Deer_Valley_Resort_logo.svg/330px-Deer_Valley_Resort_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Valley"},{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Deervalleyutah_0209.jpg/500px-Deervalleyutah_0209.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Deervalleyutah_0209.jpg/500px-Deervalleyutah_0209.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeervalleyutah_0209.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/1280px-The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-The_St_Regis_hotel_tram_at_Deer_Valley_in_Park_City_Utah_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The St. Regis Resort at Deer Valley